@startuml Maintenance Participant Diagram
title Figure X: Maintenance Task Completion Participant Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #fff9e6
    BorderColor #d4a017
    FontSize 11
}

actor "Maintenance Staff" as User
participant "Maintenance Page" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "SupabaseMaintenanceService" as Service <<Control>>
database "Maintenance Tasks" as Tasks <<Database>>
database "Maintenance History" as History <<Database>>
database "Maintenance Stats" as Stats <<Database>>

autonumber

User -> UI : Mark Task as Completed (Input Notes, Cost)
activate UI

UI -> Service : completeTask(taskId, completionData)
activate Service

Service -> Tasks : Update Status & Next Due Date
activate Tasks
Tasks --> Service : Success
deactivate Tasks

Service -> History : Insert Completion Record
activate History
History --> Service : Success
deactivate History

Service -> Stats : Update/Insert Monthly Stats
activate Stats
Stats --> Service : Success
deactivate Stats

Service --> UI : { updatedTask, historyEntry }
deactivate Service

UI -> UI : Refresh Local State & Stats
UI --> User : Display Success Toast & Update List
deactivate UI

note right of Service
  **Atomic Update:**
  The service ensures that
  task status, audit history,
  and KPI stats are all 
  synchronized in one flow.
end note

@enduml
